 :measurements-asked
 {:M1 "THE CARRIERS, each INHABITED BY A FINDER, not by a hand-built receipt.
       Slice 4's review had to strengthen exactly this (a Prop carries no WHICH,
       and a hand-built receipt is not a finder). For each candidate carrier of
       the citation datum, give a finder over the recorded repository
       (findSnatchRepository, mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11Conformance.lean
       :35-38) and prove its selection NONEMPTY on a named recorded input before
       any claim about it counts."
  :M2 "THE SEPARATION, and its ERASURE. For each carrier that claims to buy
       something, prove BOTH that it separates a citing from a misciting finder
       AND that the two are EQUAL after erasure to today's FindResult -- the pair
       is what makes it a BUY rather than a difference (the shape at
       mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:340 and :351). A
       separation without its erasure is not a measurement of today's carrier."
  :M3 "THE REFUTER, ADJUDICATED IN LEAN IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. Does the priced
       AmendedReceipt (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11AmendedCarrier.lean:18-21)
       at slice 6's instantiation state CitesTheSelectedPattern
       (mathlib4 DarkTower/WarMachine/F11NonSelfCertifying.lean:267-269)? Prove
       it or refute it. Then ask the independence question the other way: is
       there a finder pair separated by the citation datum and NOT by the
       acknowledged clause, and a pair separated by the acknowledged clause and
       NOT by the citation datum? Two theorems, one each way, or a proof that one
       direction fails."
